course: dictionary
lesson: 3823
title: Words for machines at work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen, but you can often work them out from the words around them. «A forklift truck lifts pallets on two steel forks.» Pallets are things that goods sit on, and the forks lift them, so a forklift must be something that lifts heavy things.
explain: Look for clues in the rest of the sentence too. «Keep to the marked walkways and never stand under a raised load.» People stay well away from a lifted load, so a forklift is a machine that can be dangerous to stand near when it is working.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The forklift driver lifted the boxes onto the high shelf.» Put in "a small, strong vehicle with forks" and it still makes sense, so that is the meaning. Drivers need special training to use one safely.
fact: A forklift is a small, strong vehicle with two long metal prongs at the front.
fact: The prongs, called forks, slide under heavy loads to lift and move them.
fact: Forklifts are used in warehouses, factories, supermarkets and ports.
fact: «Forklift truck» means the same as forklift.
fact: A heavy counterweight at the back stops a forklift tipping forward.
exercise: «A forklift truck lifts pallets on two steel forks.» What does a forklift do? | It grows fruit in the warehouse | It carries people to school | It cleans the floor | *It lifts and moves heavy loads
exercise: In the lesson, a pallet is something a forklift lifts. What is a pallet most likely to be? | A type of ship | *A flat base that goods are stacked on | A kind of hat | A small pet
exercise: Why do people keep to the marked walkways near a forklift? | *So they stay safe from moving machines | To race the forklift to the shelves | Because the walkways are painted for fun | To get a better view of the stock
test: «A forklift truck lifts pallets on two steel forks.» Which word tells you what the forks are made of? | truck | pallets | *steel | lifts
test: Jade says forklift is a new word. What is the best strategy? | *Read the words around it, then check by swapping in your meaning | Stop reading and never read again | Ask no one and ignore it | Guess a random meaning and move on
exam: What is a forklift? | A tall tree in a park | A type of bread | A large boat for the sea | *A small, strong vehicle with two long metal prongs that lifts heavy loads
